172
00:12:14,993 --> 00:12:28,197
attorney Jonathan Silverstein with us, and he's going to do a little bit of an overview of what we're looking at, a bit about the ordinance, some very high-level training before we begin.

173
00:12:28,217 --> 00:12:32,458
Good evening.

174
00:12:32,478 --> 00:12:33,219
Can everyone hear me?

175
00:12:34,079 --> 00:12:34,319
Yes.

176
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:36,200
Great.

177
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:40,379
As you said, Madam Chair, this is Jonathan Silberstein.

178
00:12:40,399 --> 00:12:45,622
I am outside counsel for the city on cannabis related matters.

179
00:12:46,503 --> 00:12:59,770
And primarily, I just wanted to make sure that members of the board had all the information they needed to hear the first special permit application, which obviously is coming up next.

180
00:13:00,270 --> 00:13:06,213
I'll give you, as you said, a very high level sort of summary of the zoning

181
00:13:06,854 --> 00:13:11,556
that was adopted by the city to permit marijuana businesses.

182
00:13:12,156 --> 00:13:22,520
And then obviously, if members of the board have any questions, I'm happy to answer those either now or during the course of the public hearing on the next application to come up.

183
00:13:23,581 --> 00:13:32,884
So a year or so ago, the council passed specific zoning to deal with marijuana businesses.

184
00:13:34,782 --> 00:13:41,545
which is allowed under the state statute chapter 94G, which deals with cannabis related businesses.

185
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:49,948
And that is found in section 14-523 is the special permit provisions.

186
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:50,969
And

187
00:13:58,538 --> 00:14:20,810
In addition to the traditional special permit criteria, which still apply to a special permit application for a marijuana business, there are a number of different findings that the board is called upon to make with respect to a marijuana business, and then a number of conditions that the applicant has to demonstrate compliance with.

188
00:14:21,890 --> 00:14:27,393
Most of those are operational conditions and track pretty closely with

189
00:14:28,002 --> 00:14:37,771
what the state statute says and with what the state agency's regulations, the state agency that deals with this is the Cannabis Control Commission.

190
00:14:39,392 --> 00:14:42,175
So the city didn't look to reinvent the wheel here.

191
00:14:43,136 --> 00:14:48,500
By and large, it, as I said, tracks closely to what the state requirements are.

192
00:14:49,801 --> 00:14:54,526
There are some specific provisions that relate to

193
00:14:56,106 --> 00:15:07,835
hours of operation, prohibiting drive-through services, outside signage, and the requirement for a host community agreement.

194
00:15:07,975 --> 00:15:13,058
And I will say that the upcoming applicant does have an executed host community agreement with the mayor.

195
00:15:15,019 --> 00:15:19,202
So there are specific

196
00:15:22,205 --> 00:15:37,396
filings that the applicants required to submit with its application including a security plan that has been submitted to the police chief, an operation and management plan, an emergency response plan, and an odor control plan.

197
00:15:37,876 --> 00:15:42,419
I will say that odor control is not frequently an issue with retail establishments.

198
00:15:42,499 --> 00:15:47,523
It's more often a concern with cultivation and manufacturing establishments.

199
00:15:50,888 --> 00:16:07,293
The special permit findings that the board is supposed to make, in addition to the general special permit filing findings in section 9481 are listed in section 14-526.

200
00:16:09,334 --> 00:16:11,615
And I won't list them all.

201
00:16:11,675 --> 00:16:18,097
There are a number of them, but again, most of them track pretty closely to

202
00:16:19,409 --> 00:16:21,910
the statute and the state regulations.

203
00:16:23,251 --> 00:16:36,757
And they essentially are intended to ensure that specific impacts that are sometimes concerns with marijuana establishments are addressed in the application.

204
00:16:37,477 --> 00:16:46,162
So things like odor control, security, minimizing

205
00:16:47,828 --> 00:16:53,989
risks of improper disposal of marijuana product.

206
00:16:54,949 --> 00:16:57,350
And those, again, are all listed in the ordinance.

207
00:17:00,050 --> 00:17:07,631
The applicant has entered into a very detailed host community agreement with the mayor, as I mentioned.

208
00:17:07,651 --> 00:17:10,472
I think the members of the board should have that.

209
00:17:10,492 --> 00:17:13,612
I'm happy to answer any questions that may arise with respect to that HCA.

210
00:17:17,252 --> 00:17:29,097
And then there are a few specific provisions that relate to particular types of marijuana establishments, in this case, retailers.

211
00:17:29,237 --> 00:17:41,642
So in 527E, there are six specific provisions that are intended to control marijuana retail operations.

212
00:17:43,865 --> 00:17:54,512
One is a limitation on the number to 20%, no more than 20% of the licenses for on-premises liquor licenses.

213
00:17:56,373 --> 00:18:01,816
This is obviously the first retail license that you have or retail special permit application you have in front of you.

214
00:18:01,836 --> 00:18:04,618
So there's no issue with respect to that provision.

215
00:18:04,638 --> 00:18:09,421
A requirement to comply with the regulations of the Cannabis Control Commission.

216
00:18:09,461 --> 00:18:11,902
Of course, the applicant will be required to do that.

217
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:20,004
I just have a question on what you just said about the 20%.

218
00:18:21,224 --> 00:18:27,485
I saw that in ordinance as a city council passed it, they limited it to three total.

219
00:18:30,006 --> 00:18:41,548
Is there any, I'm just curious, I didn't see when I was reviewing all of the paperwork, anything that said that essentially how we would make a determination as to those, is it just,

220
00:18:42,193 --> 00:18:43,414
first come first serve.

221
00:18:43,534 --> 00:18:52,081
And then if there are three establishments or that 20% and someone else applies, that we just say that the limit has been reached.

222
00:18:52,502 --> 00:18:54,503
